SSD (chunked state-space duality) Mamba-2 prefill on CDNA

Re-cut against upstream 030ebb558 (2026-08-10). Upstream restructured the
CUDA MMQ config into ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq-config-cdna.cuh, which broke the
old 04/05/06/07 patch boundaries; 04 and 07 both edited ssm-scan.cu, so they
are consolidated here. The chunk-size tunable formerly shipped as patch 07
(SSM_SSD_CHUNK_SIZE 256 -> 128, worth +2.5% on rocBLAS) is now the first hunk
below.

Upstream gates the SSD prefill path two ways: a preprocessor guard around both
kernels and dispatch, and a runtime capability test. This admits HIP to the
guards and widens the runtime test with GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_CDNA(cc), leaving
NVIDIA's condition byte-for-byte unchanged. Deliberately CDNA only -- RDNA's
WMMA tile shapes are unvalidated here, and MUSA stays excluded.

Measured on 2x MI210 (gfx90a), Nemotron-3-Super-120B-A12B:
  pp4096  1366 -> 1624 t/s (+18.9%)
  pp16384 1775 -> 2114 t/s (+19.1%)
  ssm_scan_f32_group: 22.8% of GPU time -> 1.0%
Gate: test-backend-ops -o SSM_SCAN, 7/7 on both devices, including multi-chunk
and non-multiple-of-chunk shapes.

